is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T08:30:00-07:00","id":188729,"title":"","content":"Yeah I noticed that too, especially Blake's ear which looked absolutely abysmal in Volume 1 but the trailer they looked much, much better.<br /> <br /> You know between the trailer and the lyrics of the opening song for this season I get the feeling that things are going to get... well not dark but definitely deeper and more grim than Volume 1. Volume 1 was very much character and world building, we got indications of the villains and the serious stuff going on in the world but they were off to side. Volume 2 looks like it could be the beginning of the story proper.<br /> <br /> Having watched the trailer several times now I actually more interested in that opening scene with Ozpin and the white suit man. It's pretty clear that White Suit's either a military officer or a politician. Him bringing a military presence to Beacon is interesting as is his exchange with Ozpin. At first thought he was talking about a war with White Fang and the Faunus but now I'm starting to think that it may not be the case. If the military wanted to make a big show to intimidate the White Fang wouldn't a show in the City of Vale itself be a more logical choice? Unless it isn't a show of force for the White Fang but rather the students arriving from the other nations for the tournament.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:09:08-07:00","id":188767,"title":"","content":"Add in the fact that White Fang's, well, a terrorist group. You make a big show, they scatter and leave bombs. Those sort of things don't impress them, they invite targets.<br /> <br /> Still, we don't know enough about the other nations to know what would invite War with...Gah, names names names. Is the world called Remnant or Vytal, and if it's Remnant, is Vytal the country? EDIT: Remnant is the world, Vytal is the continent, Vale is the country, and has the city of Vale within it's borders. Cleared that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2014, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:45:33-07:00","id":188781,"title":"","content":"True though in the panel they did mention they were going to explain more about the world.<br /> <br /> But given that we do know the White Fang is working with Torchwick and his boss, Cinder Fall, and that her subordinates/teammates Mercury and Emerald are competing in the tournament it is possible that Torchwick and the White Fang are being manipulated by outside forces bent on undermining and weakening Vale as part of the precursor to a war. Or maybe White Suit just believes that. It could be part of Cinder's overall plan.<br /> <br /> Of course that's just one possibility based on what facts we do know. It could be that Cinder, Torchwick and the White Fang are all working for White Suit as part of some greater plot of his. We'll just have to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:50:32-07:00","id":188784,"title":"","content":"<i>Do</i> we know Mercury and Emerald are competing in the tournament?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T10:34:43-07:00","id":188801,"title":"","content":"The RWBY clip at the end of the Lazer Team livestream they did last month. The clip showed Mercury fighting Pyrrha in an arena while others, including Ruby and Emerald, watched. Emerald even acted polite and friendly to Ruby. I say acted as the moment Ruby turned away she rolled her eyes.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's safe to assume they're in the tournament. Also if you're wondering Mercury's weapons are a pair of boots and greaves similar to Yang's Ember Celica though they didn't give us much of a showing of what they're capable of.<br /> <br /> I saw the livestream but haven't seen the clip since, even among the videos people made of the livestream and posted online so I can't really direct you to a video of it if you missed it. The best I can do is direct you to their image gallery pages on the RWBY wiki which does have pictures from the clip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:23:55-07:00","id":207468,"title":"","content":"So, just a few hours left to the season two premiere (01:00 GMT), less for members (00:30 GMT) and even less for sponsors (23:00 GMT). At least I <i>think</i> those are the times...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm hyped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:25:52-07:00","id":207470,"title":"","content":"I was going to bump it when I got it.<br /> <br /> I am a sponsor, so early thoughts are a coming, despite moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:08:27-07:00","id":207587,"title":"","content":"First step to getting the sponsor view: actually log in to your sponsor account. Gah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:56:02-07:00","id":207617,"title":"","content":"Okay, that? Was awesome. I have nothing more to say.<br /> <br /> Turns out I lied. But it's not that interesting, because it's just me saying how everything was awesome. And really, what a terrific way to start off a season. It was dominated by humour and combat choreography in blessed union, which are two of the strongest points of the series. Add to this the great voice acting, the vastly improved animation (is it just me, or did they add proper shadows?), the glory of a full 15 minutes and the story hooks spread throughout, it's... just great. Just great.<br /> <br /> See? That was boring, generic praise. I'll try some more specific praise.<br /> <br /> Mercury and Emerald make an interesting team and they get some good lines. I like the intimidation scene in the book shop; the way Mercury slams the books are subtly threatening, and I'm giddy at the implication that the Third Crusade book might represent some sort of secret manifesto or code. I hope it becomes relevant again, but then, I just like it when books are made significant.<br /> <br /> Best line #1:<br /> <b>Ruby:</b> &quot;Sisters! Friends! ...Weiss.&quot;<br /> <b>Weiss:</b> &quot;HEY!&quot;<br /> <b>Ruby:</b> &quot;Four-score and seven minutes ago, I had a dream.&quot;<br /> <b>Yang:</b> &quot;This ought to be good.&quot;<br /> <br /> The guy with the blue hair... I'm not sure about him. My first reaction is that he'll either be a douche or a traitor. Seriously, just look at him. He's way to handsome to not be evil.<br /> <br /> Best line #2:<br /> <b>Ruby:</b> &quot;Justice will be swift! Justice will be painful! IT WILL BE DELICIOUS!&quot;<br /> <br /> Not really a line, but one of the best moments in the episode is when Weiss does her Myrtenaster dash with a swordfish. I had to pause and laugh for a full minute.<br /> <br /> I actually have one problem with this episode, though, namely the ending of the combat. I'm not entirely sure I understand what Ruby did there. Sure, we know she's fast, but she's never been <i>that</i> much about <i>pure speed</i>. That was some Sonic the Hedgehog shit. I'm not sure I really buy it. It felt like they needed Ruby to end it and couldn't really find a way that didn't involve Crescent Rose.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Awesome episode. I'm already waiting for the next one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:02:10-07:00","id":207620,"title":"","content":"I know right?<br /> <br /> So, RWBY Volume 2: Best Day Ever.<br /> <br /> The moral of the story is that Nora can kick everyone's ass in a food fight. Also, someone needs to talk to Beacon's food staff, because that's kind of gross.<br /> <br /> It's been a whole year since RWBY came onto the scene, and certainly my opinion of the show has been very mixed. I'm not the only one, lots of reviewers don't know if it's a really well made amateur show or a poor professional one, which I think says more about Rooster Teeth as a company than on RWBY. I think I concluded that while the story and episode focus was lacking, and while a lot of it is not innovative, there is an incredible heart and joy to the show that makes it infectious, and I have no problems saying that I have become warmer to the show over the year. It's just fun. But I had really been wanting to see improvements.<br /> <br /> As openers goes, this shows off the best of both worlds-that incredible heart and fun mixed in with some solid improvements.<br /> <br /> First, the animation. THere's...shading. And texture. And Gradients, and a whole lot of other things I hadn't noticed were missing from the first volume, lots of little things and improvements on stuff that was there. This show already looked fairly nice in a stylized way, but now it feels a little more grounded and fully spruced up. There's a vividness and light to it all in just the right places, and it feels less like a slightly poor turn of the millennium cell shaded art piece now and very definitely more akin to today's level of 3D. Again, it looked good before, but now the entire look and style just is more...more. And the fluidity of motion is also fairly solid, a little more naturalistic in the not-combat scenes. It's hard to articulate al the ways it actually looks better, because it still looks a lot like RWBY, but it looks better, it looks fresher.<br /> <br /> Sound wise, the show it also good. I expected the characters who were here before to really be settled in their roles, and they are, and there were some really fun lines on their part. The thing that impresses me most was the new voice actors for Neptune, Mercury and Emerald though, as they sound like they've been doing this for ages. I'll talk more on the characters later, but suffice it to say these guys are again very naturalistic, and clearly having fun with their roles. The bookshop owner, thouhg, well, he's standard for the &quot;I'm not important&quot; roles of RWBY. He...said lines.<br /> <br /> WHile the story really hasn't started yet, it now feels like something <i>happened</i> last volume, and that's thanks to the show half-focus on the villains. In fact, that's probably my favorite part about this episode. Our villains feel human and relatable, although not sympathetic(which isn't bad, mind), and what's more is that I really believe they are up to something. We really, truly see the culmination of what Roman was up to last semester, and that sense of scale promises the scale for this one. Enough small things have happened to create an explosion, and the villains, while still unclear in their goals, feel potent in a way they never felt before. What's more is their dynamics. Again, I'll talk characters later, but these guys have a great dysfunctional group of friends feel already without losing the sense that Cinder, Mercury, and Emerald would kill-and do worse- for what they want. Roman remains lovably weasely, and the major problem in their little group. But best of all, despite a solid guess with Roman(That honestly had been there since the end of the last volume), I have no idea where the story is going to go with these guys.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, I've refrained from the meat of the episode long enough. Monty starts RWBY off with what Monty does best-explain characters through a badass fight. Thing of the matter is that it's a food fight, and the entire damn thing is ridiculous as hell. They're beating each other up with leeks and french bread and turkey boxing gloves. It's a huge big ball of ROFLOMGWTF. Everything you need to know is just communicated through this fight.<br /> <br /> I don't have anything else to say, and in fact I don't have much to say on the characters, except to say that there's not a one I dislike. I want to see more.<br /> <br /> We're off to a good start folks. Everything you love is here, and everything that was wrong seems to have at least been sanded down.<br /> <br /> Best Line goes to Ruby and Weiss for &quot;Sisters! Friends!...Weiss.&quot;&quot;Hey!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:48:39-07:00","id":207703,"title":"","content":"Actually, you know what, I do have another thing to say.<br /> <br /> Dialogue. Holy shit, the dialogue.<br /> <br /> RWBY has never had terrible dialogue, but I can't accuse it of always being...interesting. A lot of the time, things were being said, and they were good to know, but that was about it. Best Day Ever has fantastic dialogue, with great point-counter point timing and characteristic styling. This shines again really nicely with the scene before the fight, because the humor runs quick and steady, but the villain scenes are so much fun to watch because the dialogue is just so on point with it's wording and it's delivery. It's fun to listen to even the more mundane parts of the episode(not it has much in the way of that). So, yeah, holy shit that dialogue.<br /> <br /> Also, while I still don't have a lot ot say, I really like how the thing with the White Fang from the last episode is weighing on Blake's mind. I really just want to give the poor girl a hug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:14:05-07:00","id":207768,"title":"","content":"Quite an enjoyable episode. While you could see the animation improving over the course of the first season but the improvement they've made between seasons... wow. The trailers and the clips looked great but actually seeing an episode with more of the non-action scenes and a chance to really see the fine details is a whole other matter. The smaller character movements, which had been an issue in the first season, are now much smoother while the details of the character models have noticeably improved. For instance Blake's eyes have gained a more cat-like shape. And man is it refreshing to see background characters that are actual characters and not black silhouettes.<br /> <br /> The dialogue's about the same as we've come to expect though I have to admit I am a little disappointed that we didn't get much actual stuff from Team RWBY. Don't get me wrong I'm more and more intrigued by what Cinder, Torchwick and Co. are doing and the bit with Ruby and others was funny but I would have liked something a little more substantial from them. Plus it was largely from a previously released clip so it was also kind of old for me.<br /> <br /> And that food fight... seriously what else needs to be said. Teams RWBY and JNPR fighting each other with mock weapons made from food. We've seen plenty of hilarious things in RWBY and plenty of epic things but this was one of those hilariously epic moments. Or an epically hilarious moment. With RWBY the line between epiciness and hilarity can be ripped out entirely and shot out of Nora's Magnhild.<br /> <br /> All and all a pretty good episode and a solid start to the new season. Can't wait for next week.<br /> <br /> Also anyone else notice the sketch of Adam from the Black trailer in Blake's notebook. Got to wonder, given the apparent emphasis on the White Fang we've seen the in trailer, are we going to see him in this season?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:28:19-07:00","id":207814,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the black silhouettes , but I'm a diehard for Utena, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:30:16-07:00","id":207975,"title":"","content":"I didn't mind the black silhouettes, but I'm not mourning them either. I think it's better with proper people.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Blake confront Adam. I want to know what their relationship was before Blake left.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T15:13:53-07:00","id":215106,"title":"","content":"So it's come to my attention that the Exalted Forums have an extensive RWBY Forum over there. To that, I have to say: Shame on you. I thought when they shunted both the old RWBY and the MLP threads over into here the lesson was learned.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not just bitter because they have way more conversation going on than we do. Even though I am.<br /> <br /> So, RWBY Volume 2, Episode 2: Welcome to Beacon.<br /> <br /> Hey, look! The plot is both thickening <i>and </i>moving!<br /> <br /> It also makes zero sense at this point. But let's get technicals out of the way first.<br /> <br /> So the animation has gone back into more humor filled territory-er, more of the standard material, rather than a comedic fight of ages, as it were- and....I'm not sure why it works, but it works. THe usual issues with a lack of stretch and squash and handling of snap didn't come in here, and I think a large part of that came from how they decided to handle it. The scene with Weiss in particular felt like an embrace of the medium's issues, and when it's used as an effect rather than a byproduct, it...works. I feel really weird saying that. I'm not saying i's great, but it does work.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say on the audio, so....characters.<br /> <br /> Before individuals, I feel like I must say that things feels more like the result of relationships rather than individuals now, which makes going through the large list of characters already here a bit of a struggle. It's an improvement in general from last volume-not because the characterization was bad there, but because this is much more layered and real. THe verisimilitude is here as peanut butter mortar, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> Ozpin has been a favorite for a while now, and largely remains so here. He's been given a little bit more to work with, and the man is starting to be fleshed out. I know some key moments in his career are sure toe come up, but what I love about him is that so far he hasn't needed those pin points-it's enough to say that he has led many, seen many die, and killed much in his life. It's been great to see him walk with that and to talk with that, but now we see how he responds to it, and interestingly enough, he comes off as a competent Cornelius Fudge from <i>Harry Potter</i>. He just wants peace, and while he's not closing his eyes to it, he's not about to start riling people up over it yet because he wants peace, and he wants people to enjoy peace. He's not wrong....but he might not be right either. It's a nifty twist.<br /> <br /> Glinda's role as the hardass comes more and more into perspective with this context. Ozpin and Ironwood(more on him in a second) are both fairly thoughtful men, and even though Ironwood is more active, I never got the impression he hadn't carefully gauged his options-but Glinda exists in context of Ozpin, so let's get back to that. Where Ozpin debates and struggles, Glinda has to be the one who draws lines. She does so at Ozpin's behest, but I think her being a hardass and turning the path he takes into iron edicts is just as much for his sake as it is a sign for her loyalty. Ozpin is mutable in his own way, and he needs someone who at least looks like iron to back him, and Glinda does that. She doesn't waver anywhere, because he's always got an eye somewhere, and if he saw her not be the strong pillar, it might allow his more questioning nature lead to inaction and/or reversal of action.<br /> <br /> Ironwood strikes me as a middle of the road to these two. A man of sorrows like Ozpin, he also thinks long and hard about what to do, and probably doesn't see any clear answers either. Lacking a Glinda in his life though, he's had to become the one who makes the push in his life-he's had be his own iron when he plays more like Ozpin's wet clay. People like that often feel pushed into decisions because of the need to do something, and they often make bad choices because of the sense of haste. It doesn't help he's got some serious positions. He may be an academy leader, but he's also openly a general-unlike Ozpin who chose to be a clay shaper, Ironwood is a metalshaper, he has to force things into place hard. THe conclusion he's made feels organic to what I think is his nature. He's not making the right choice either, but it's not wrong either. Both he and Ozpin are going to have their choices bite them in the ass in their own ways-to be fair, it's not a situation that has an answer that doesn't bite.<br /> <br /> The entire Risk board game scene was cute, and fun, and I love seeing RWBY have fun as a group...the problem being that it's not, but more on that in a second. For now, Ruby and Yang's sisterly dynamics are awesome to watch and, again, true to life. Weiss's involvment with the game is also familiar to me, as I've been there on several games of Magic the Gathering, and seeing two people who know go at it while the third one ambitiously tries to win but has no clue what they're doing is just true to life and adorable to boot. JNPR didn't do much, but their contributions were funny all the same. By the way, shout out to X-Ray and Vav, who will be getting their own series later on, and a few other jokes I can't remember right now.<br /> <br /> So remember how I was going on about how Jaune never made himself appealing in the last scene, and thus Pyrrha's interest in him couldn't be romantic? While I conceeded that it might have been romantic, I still stand by that, and Neptune(the real reason I bring this up) is the reason why. I grant that he was not amazingly charming, but he was smoother and more respectable, so when he goes &quot;snow angel&quot; to Weiss and she doesn't go nutso, I buy it. I don't think she's taken with him(although that may change and build), but she's not offended by him either, and at least finds it minorly endearing. I'm not sold that he's as smooth and suave as I think the show wants me to believe, but the man has earned what he's put out, and I wouldn't be surprised if he came to be more so. Do I think he's up to something? No, I think he's just a player, but I think he'll be fun to watch.<br /> <br /> More Sun. Now. I find it particularly cute how he's trying to warm up to Blake, and that's that.<br /> <br /> So, onto Team RWBY proper. Gotta start with Blake.<br /> <br /> Oh Blake. Oh Blake.<br /> <br /> Once again, it's great that out of everyone, she's the one carrying the baggage from the last season, because of course she does-she thinks wider than everyone else and sits on things a lot more(With the exception of maybe Weiss, but she at least keeps going with something while brooding), and I love how her instincts are still to run and hide. She doesn't trust, well, anyone-Ozpin's interview shows that much. I like that she doesn't share anything with him for a lot of reasons.<br /> <br /> That said, <i>you stupid, stupid person</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't say that as a slam on her, it makes sense-but this is really a situation where showing your cards <i>helps</i>. I get why, but it is still mildly frustrating that she does it She needed to let out that explosion of concern, if nothing else. Passing on her htughts and knowledge would have been a big help. I'm also a little appalled at her arrogance-maybe no one knows the White Fang like she does, but that's crass to assume <i>Ozpin</i> doesn't know a hefty helping. More to the point, if people don't know, <i>tell them!</i><br /> <br /> Thankfully, Weiss is here to call bullshit.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall bitching a tong about Weiss last volume. I really wanted to like her, and her intro made that really hard. Still, she is probably my second favorite character, and it's for stuff like this that has been creeping out over time-in fact, now it's in full bloom. I'm <i>so glad</i> it was Weiss who called Blake out, <i>particularly</i> given their last conversation. Weiss has her bag of issues, but she's self-aware in a way that Yang and Ruby just aren't(although not as much as Blake, Weiss clearly shows blindspots) and really just aware in a way many of them aren't. She cuts to the point, with others and herself, and she makes her points solidly(With a <i>great </i>chair balancing act to boot).<br /> <br /> I also kind of like how she's the cautious one(HOORAY FOR TAKING RESPONSIBILITY AS A MAGE!). She's book smart in ways where the others are street smart, and while her education was not gentle in the way book-smart normally works, her objectivity on most of the world is still from the viewpoint of a glass tower. She is calculated without a great sense of what really happens in the situations those calculations are based on. Where Blake feels the concern and Ruby and Yang feel the drive to do something about it, Weiss reins them in a bit and keeps them grounded. Her role as second lead to RWBY is coming in nicely, and I like that, even if it is a problem in this scenario.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Ruby, this is her story, right? Yeah, it is. Where Blake worried about a problem bigger than her and Weiss enforced that, Ruby wisely said &quot;Screw that, we know, therefore we do&quot;(not an actual quote). They might not be able to do much, but they can do something.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't include <i>talking to Ozpin</i>, but we'll let that slide for now.<br /> <br /> Again, Ruby is taking charge, and it's cool the see that. The team really is coming together, and I'm curious how it'll go.<br /> <br /> Yang. Remember last volume how I said with Yang &quot;What you see is what you get&quot;? I'm getting more of the same here. Yang isn't showing more or growing like the others are, and I still can't decide if that's a good thing or a bad thing. We'll see. Otherwise? Hilarious as always.<br /> <br /> And that leaves me with the stinger.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...No.<br /> <br /> Not for a second.<br /> <br /> Don't buy it.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing-I don't believe you could <i>ever </i>pass off Cinder as a student. Maybe Mercury and Emerald? But not Cinder. Cinder's just too...mature.<br /> <br /> I know how that sounds, shut up. What I mean is that, while we are dealing with young adults, the characters are still children in their way. Cinder <i>isn't</i>. Cinder <i>so isn't</i>. Anyone looking with eyes can see that-anyone with a brain <i>knows</i> that. This entire charade doesn't work in my head.<br /> <br /> And in fact, I think it's crazy to think that Qrow, Ozpin, and Ironwood can talk about their enemies(Queens has pawns, anyone) without knowing what they look like! Or at the least, what Cinder looks like!<br /> <br /> As for the plot, well...I don't like where it's saying it's going, but I'll let it slide. Rant rant, bitch bitch later if I'm vindicated.<br /> <br /> All in all though, good episode, I loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T06:10:58-07:00","id":215795,"title":"","content":"It's been a week already? I have to catch up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:53:46-07:00","id":215857,"title":"","content":"Watched the episode a couple times and gotta to say it was a pretty solid episode. No action but some interesting developments.<br /> <br /> We finally learn who Mister White Suit is, General James Ironwood from Atlas. So far he's about what I expected from the trailer which isn't a bad thing as I now get an even greater sense that there's a connection between him and Cinder. That's not to say they are working together cause I don't think they are, rather I don't think its a coincidence that she's had Torchwick's group and the White Fang terrorizing Vale on the eve of the Vytal Festival where people from all over the Four Kingdoms are going to be there or that Ironwood has responded by bringing a sizable military force with him and his students. How that will play out I can only guess at this point.<br /> <br /> But I did notice some interesting things about Ironwood. First off the second time I watched the episode I notice something in the opening credits, a brief image among the rapid shots of the various teams and groups. It took me a few tries but to my surprise it was Ironwood and his group, which consisted of a bunch of those new soldier robots we saw in the trailer, a pair of soldiers, two younger people who are likely students from Atlas and Penny. So Penny's from Atlas. But what's really interesting is her posture compared to the others. Ironwood and the others are standing very much like in a military lineup but Penny isn't rather she looks nervous or apprehensive, like she doesn't want to be there. I wonder what that could mean...<br /> <br /> And anyone else thinking Ironwood has at the very least a cybernetic hand?<br /> <br /> I did love the scene with Team RWBY playing Remnant the Game*. It was a great balance to the more serious half of the episode. As for the rest of it, I largely agree with Arcane's thoughts. The one thing I do have to disagree with Arcane here on is Cinder. While I do kind of agree on strangeness of Cinder posing student I also have to admit that I find the same for several of the other students we've seen, especially Pyrrah who looks, sounds and feels older compared to everyone else. So I can accept that. No, what I disagree with is the notion that Qrow, Ozpin and Ironwood must know who Cinder is. First off we don't exactly know the extent of their knowledge, the context of Qrow's message or even a remote idea on Cinder's plans. At this point all we can do is speculate and theorize. At this point we're assuming that the 'Queen' in Qrow's message is Cinder but we can't actually say for sure. What if she isn't? What if Qrow is talking about someone or something we haven't seen yet? <br /> <br /> Secondly do we actually know they have seen Cinder one way or another? Yes, Glynda did see Cinder in the first episode of Volume 1 but her face was shadowed at that time and given how she appeared to act as a subordinate to Torchwick muddling up who exactly she was to them. In fact when I first saw Cinder period I assumed she was the middleman between Torchwick and the real Big Bad. And you know what, I still kind of do.<br /> <br /> Until we know more about the whole situation we can't say for certain on anything with Cinder or Qrow's message.<br /> <br /> *Someone needs to get out there and make that game a real thing. If Roosterteeth doesn't, the fans will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:57:48-07:00","id":215860,"title":"","content":"I grant that I'm stretching on the second one, but if Ozpin turns out to be surprised, I'll be equally surprised.<br /> <br /> As for the maturity factor...Hmm. The average age is actually 17, so....<br /> <br /> Nope, still don't buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T15:23:40-07:00","id":221283,"title":"","content":"New episode of RWBY came out!<br /> <br /> I need to buy a bookshelfthough, so no full review yet. The nutshell though?<br /> <br /> This Volume of RWBY keeps knocking it out of the park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T18:21:26-07:00","id":221387,"title":"","content":"Another Thursday and another new episode. First off we get the return of Professor Port and Jaune trying, unsuccessfully, to score with Weiss. And I loved seeing them both return, it gives us a nice sense of continuity with Volume One which in terms of the story's timeline wasn't that long ago. Plus it was an amusing scene.<br /> <br /> Then we get the girls in their room getting ready to investigate Torchwick, the White Fang and what they could be planning. I got to say that this scene and the one after it really made me notice just how much better they've gotten on the smaller movements they had problems with last season. Also having the team in another set of clothes besides their combat clothes and school uniforms was a nice touch. One of the little things that has annoyed me about other animes is how the characters at best have two, maybe three sets of clothes.<br /> <br /> As for the scene itself, hilarious as always. As always the people at Roosterteeth know their comedy. I have to admit when Sun first appeared in the window and said &quot;It's easy, I do it all the time.&quot; my mind immediately thought it was going to go in an entirely different direction, thoughts that it seems Weiss was also thinking if her reaction is any indication. And Neptune, Neptune, Neptune... we know next to nothing about you but I love you interactions with everybody.<br /> <br /> After that we get the return of Penny and further proof that she's a gender-flipped Pinocchio, her hiccuping while she attempts to lie to Ruby and Weiss. But more importantly we get more insight in Weiss and her past. I really loved how when Weiss was in the elevator she was psyching herself up for calling the HQ of the family business and how during the call itself she was smiling politely but as soon as the call ended she frowned. It all adds to what we already know about Weiss, she didn't have the greatest childhood. And it has some interesting implications for the new bit of info we did learn about her. She's from Atlas yet going to school in another Kingdom. To escape from her father or is there something more to it? Regardless it's been hinted at since the White Trailer that she did not have a happy past and I've always been curious about that. Hopefully as we did with Blake in the last season we'll get more insight into Weiss this season.<br /> <br /> Then we get Ruby and Penny talking. There's isn't much to their conversation save for the very end where Penny reveals that someone *cough*Ironwood*cough* doesn't want her talking with people. Which leads us into Ironwood advertising the new Elysium Knights and Paladin. And surprise surprise it's the big mech that we saw the White Fang using in the trailer. I got to say the more I see Ironside the more I'm convince there's something sinister about him. Whether he's working with (or being used by) Cinder and the White Fang towards their ends, giving them a Paladin willingly or Cinder's going to indirectly manipulate him into attacking Vale I get sense he's going to be a danger for the girls to contend with down the road.<br /> <br /> And finally there's the chase that reveals what most of us, well probably all of us, already suspected from last season, Penny being a robot. Yet despite that Penny's intense fear at revealing it and Ruby's reaction to the big reveal sold it and further goes to show just how much better the crew has become since the start of last season, both in the voice acting and in the animation. But then they leave us with a cliffhanger that likely isn't going to be answered in the next couple of episodes as they'll likely switch to Blake and Sun or Yang and Neptune for one then the other. Annoying but if nothing else Blake and Sun infiltrating a White Fang gathering or if Yang and Neptune are meeting who I think they're meeting* then it will be interesting.<br /> <br /> All and all despite being an episode of slow build up and expected reveals it was a solid, enjoyable episode. It won't be a favorite of this season but it won't be one of the laggy episodes from last season which is another good sign for this season.<br /> <br /> *My money's on Junior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:21:37-07:00","id":222457,"title":"","content":"So, RWBY Volume 2 Episode 3: A Little Hiccup.<br /> <br /> In which the little hiccup is never addressed or explained, but I think Akatsuki has it right.<br /> <br /> So since the animation, soundtrack, sound effects, and voice acting are all staying solid save for some of the weird clothes issues RWBY has always had, I'm gonna take a some time to discuss RWBY's time format and aesthetic. And by aesthetic, I mean I wanna squee and talk about the clothing, but more on that in a second.<br /> <br /> RWBY's episodes in Volume 1 were, well, irritating in their breaks. We spent weeks getting half an episode, leading to a certain clunkiness that left episodes feeling unsatisfying. Putting them together didn't really prove to be satisfying(10 episodes of roughly 12 minutes, by the way), because they still felt like they were designed to handle their short presentations on the internet. Add in some stock storytelling and it was always a little frustrating.<br /> <br /> That just makes Volume 2 even more impressive though. Each episode has been a neat balance of dense and loose. The series breathes and takes it's time as needed, but is interested in getting on quickly with that breathing pace. I feel like there's a lot of nifty character bits thrown in here that builds on each other, and since the characters are finally being realized as full and fun characters, that's rewarding as hell. The plot is going, but it's not eager to run, but given that it's so neat ot hang out with these people, it's refreshing. In short, I feel like Monty, Kerry, and Miles have really learned how to manage their time, and it has paid off.<br /> <br /> Now onto the pretty clothes. *deep breath* SQUEEEEEEEE!<br /> <br /> Let me get one thing out of the way, right now: <a href=\"http://www.dhgate.com/product/dhgate/143955765.html?utm_source=dyn&amp;utm_medium=GMC&amp;utm_campaign=dalishi&amp;utm_term=143955765&amp;f=bm%7c143955765%7c014001-UpperGarments%7cGMC%7cAdwords%7cdyn%7cdalishi%7cUS%7c014001003-Outwear%7cc%7cOSMNBH%7c&amp;gclid=CLa3ua626rkCFQeCQgod2GMAag\" target=\"_blank\">You can buy Weiss's coat</a>, so if you got a girlfriend you're trying to get into cosplay, try bribing her with this. I legitimately think it's a cute coat, so might not even need the precedent. And I wouldn't be surprised if you could find all of the other styles for sale on DHGate.<br /> <br /> If I'm really honest, I like these better than the normal outfits. Weiss's original stuff has an style I rather lie that makes me feel more neutral in regards to her, but I like how modern these are, and how more normal they seem. I realize unusual attire is part of the anime schtick and for RWBY, but seeing Blake in an outfit I legitimately thought she would wear brought so much joy to me I had a little mini-cheer. I think these are very flattering and very cool designs. I also have to agree with Akatsuki in regards to the variety factor. Anime studio budgets usually limit them to one or two designs, which is part of the reason the high school thing is as popular as it is-because one design fits all. For all of that though, we see so much of it it that we never see people realistically, well, live outside the clothes. I feel like seeing more clothing styles breathes life into the world and the characters. And if nothing else, I really do like these outfits a lot better.<br /> <br /> And no, I am not lusting after under-aged animated flesh, I really like the clothes that much.<br /> <br /> So, with that said. The events and the highlighted characters.<br /> <br /> I loved the opening classroom scene, of course. I rather like that Professor Port is like an openly mocked Gilderoy Lockhart character who's lessons are literally just self-aggrandizing stories that hide discussion of Grim creatures weaknesses and tactics against them, and I like a subtle touch of character growth on Jaune's part of trying to pick up Weiss-Old Jaune might have continued trying to overblow himself, here he tries to just appeal with activities. It's a small touch that shows that he's grown up and calmed down in some ways. One day kid, one day.<br /> <br /> The scene with the plan discussion(AWESOME CLOTHINGS SQUEEEEEEEEEEEE!) is actually fairly solid and interesting. It places Yang's trailer as squarely happening before the series(I know Monty's mentioned they all happened prior to the series, but I never believed it really), and builds on that as giving each of them solid leads to go and poke in for information. And that's another thing, these are <i>really</i> good ideas that these characters can take advantage of with their established backgrounds. THe new clothes set the tone for confronting these situations as well.<br /> <br /> Sun and Neptune continue to be awesome as hell. These two alone really make the sort of cool kids club you wish you could be a part of when you were in school. Neptune's balance of cool factor with legitimate, humanizing concern over his circumstances is just great. In fact, that's something you don't get a lot of with media-believably cool people. When you come across the cool kids in media, it's often so because the show tells you they're cool, but Sun and Neptune legitimately have earned it. The fact Neptune has done so with so little screen presence <i>astounds</i> me. Weiss is totally within her right to want to spend time with this guy. On that front, holy shit, they showed that right as well-humorous but not overblown, both feeling true to life and completely hilarious.<br /> <br /> The initial scene was, I think, a set up for future elements of the story-the Schnee's communications and transportation networks feel important in a Wild West sort of sense in that a shit ton of infrastructure seems to have been built on it. I also liked how Weiss's and Ruby's friendship has shaped out-it seems like they annoy each other, but that's part and parcel for the game, and Ruby has come to, in a way, appreciate Weiss's knowledge, and Weiss Ruby's enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> And then there was Penny, and Penny was a revelation.<br /> <br /> I didn't like Penny in Volume 1. I didn't get why people liked her so much. It boggled me. But then I saw her here and her initial claims of not knowing Ruby, and I was instantly &quot;Oh God no&quot;. And the way the characterized her from there was still stylistically that &quot;Main Street, USA from Disneyland presents an AI girl&quot;, but much more sympathetic. I'm not sure if the setup she had helped or not, but I found I could invest and care for Penny where before I didn't care.<br /> <br /> The entire scene with Weiss was to be expected, but <i>damn </i>did I love the delivery. I loved that we spent time with Weiss trying to reconcile with the call and how much she wanted to avoid her family. I like how much of it was strictly in her face, and that when it came to the call, it fit with the masks we've seen Weiss wear before-and now we know they're masks. I'm curious about her relationship with Winter.<br /> <br /> The subsequent scene with Ruby and Penny and the chase had a lot of great little moments, from Penny going through the the group as she listed who she wasn't allowed to contact, to casting some doubt on the relationships she has(she answers to her father and Ironwood, and that raises some questions in my head), to her <i>stopping</i> that truck, and Ruby's confusion and desperation, the entire thing played out like a charm.<br /> <br /> All in all, I really liked this episode, and this convinces me that Volume 2 is going to be spectaular, which is what I always wanted from RWBY.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's okay to get what you wished for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T18:02:03-07:00","id":228602,"title":"","content":"Episode Four: Painting the Town...<br /> <br /> First off, all the standard stuff. Visuals and animation, all top notch as we've been seeing thus far this season though I have to admit Yang's helmet looked...wrong but Sun's golden clones did look really good as were Blake's ears.<br /> <br /> We start off with the continuation of where we left off last time, revealing some interesting things. Penny is a robot with an Aura which would imply that she has a soul. Sounds like some of theories about Penny possibly having created after a human or being a full body cyborg might be right or at least close to the truth. And suspicions activity from Ironwood in telling Penny that the world's in danger despite being in a time of peace. Now I'm really starting to think there's some kind of connection between and Cinder's group. Worse I'm pretty sure we're going to see Penny being ordered to fight Team RWBY and it won't be pretty...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the exchange itself between the two was nice and I'm starting to like Penny more.<br /> <br /> Next up Yang and Neptune visit Junior. To begin with, this episode sold me on Neptune. In the previous episodes I was pretty indifferent to him and felt a bit like he was more of an addon to the scenes than anything else but every scene in this episode with him was hilarious. Aside from him Jack's performance as Junior was better than his showing in the Yellow trailer. And the whole reaction from Junior and his men to the return of Yang was great.<br /> <br /> Though it was strange about Junior's men. If they had been arrested you'd think he'd say that instead that they never came back...<br /> <br /> Then we got Blake and Sun infiltrating the White Fang meeting which did provide us with some interesting bits of information. The symbolism of the White Fang's mask is explained, something I never actually noticed before. Roman was...well Roman. It's always great when they have him really talk and he provides us with some insight, at least from the White Fang perspective, why they're working with him and Cinder despite hating humanity. Roman's relationship with them isn't any than he said it was, he's in business with them, selling them weapons to use against the human authorities of Vale. Oh and they got plans for things outside the city. Foreshadowing for what's to come me thinks.<br /> <br /> Also another great nod to the previous season with the faunus having better night vision.<br /> <br /> Oh, and anyone else thinking that it's unlikely that Roman could have gotten his hands on at least several brand new Paladins? Yeah, like I said I'm pretty convinced now that Ironwood's somehow connected to all this.<br /> <br /> The highway chase was... well what we've come to expect from Monty. Plus we did see such a chase before during Red vs Blue season 9.<br /> <br /> Finally the big fight between Roman in his Paladin and Team RWBY. It's the first time we've seen the girls fighting-<i>really</i> fighting-together since last year's big mid season fight and man was it impressive. We got a chance to see where the girls are at after several months together and they're shaping up to be an effective team while Ruby's definitely stepped up her game as leader, willing to standing back and take charge, directing the team like a real military leader. Also anyone else notice the battle orders Ruby was shouting out? I know at least one of them was shipping nickname and I suspect either the rest were and/or parodies of such names.<br /> <br /> And we finally learn what Yang's Semblance is, the more she gets hit the stronger she becomes to the point that she's able to destroy the Paladin's arm entire arm in single shot...<br /> <br /> Nuff said.<br /> <br /> Of course they total Roman's mech which does raise a question that if four Huntresses-in-training are able to take one of those things down, are they really going to stand a chance against full-fledged Hunters and Huntresses?<br /> <br /> Anyway we get the debut of another new henchmen. She doesn't look faunus so I'm assuming she's with Cinder, perhaps the fourth member of their team. Beyond that there's really nothing to say about her yet. But get Weiss's attempt at humor, something worthy of Barbara and Yang which makes it truly funny when Yang's the one who calls her out on how bad it is. Then we end with Sun and Neptune and another Roosterteeth reference, A Simple Wok to the noodle stand.<br /> <br /> All and all a great episode with an awesome fight scene that's certainly whetted my appetite for more.<br /> <br /> And there's something I realized as I watched this episode, we're only four episodes in and we've seen pretty much everything from the trailer... So yeah about the only things we have seen that are left are the scenes from a party at the school and what is presumably the tournament itself. A lot of unknown to come.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T20:41:00-07:00","id":228700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/185519-rwby-volume-2-discussion-thread?p=215106#post215106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, <i>you stupid, stupid person</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't say that as a slam on her, it makes sense-but this is really a situation where showing your cards <i>helps</i>. I get why, but it is still mildly frustrating that she does it She needed to let out that explosion of concern, if nothing else. Passing on her htughts and knowledge would have been a big help. I'm also a little appalled at her arrogance-maybe no one knows the White Fang like she does, but that's crass to assume <i>Ozpin</i> doesn't know a hefty helping. More to the point, if people don't know, <i>tell them!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of a difficult discussion to have though, one that leads of with &quot;I'm an Ex-Terrorist.&quot; and will have to feature selling out a large group of your species, a number of which are you former comrades in arms. To the a member of the species that is oppressing the hell out of you, no less.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:12:36-07:00","id":229262,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've been so busy a while. I might look back on the previous episodes at some point, but right now, I will just note that I agree with the criticism of Cinder's credibility as a student.<br /> <br /> So, Episode 4. Damn, that was awesome.<br /> <br /> The plot is moving ahead at a steady pace. I like the sense of progression it gives, but I'm also sort of getting a feeling that they need to get some of this stuff out of the way since the big tournament at the end will take a lot of time and it might be hard to fit plot-related development into it. Not complaining, though. Torchwick is a great charismatic villain.<br /> <br /> So we know that Penny has an Aura now, but does that mean she had a Semblance? They seem to be somehow interconnected, but I assume one doesn't have to imply the other. It might have been mentioned at some point, I forget these things.<br /> <br /> I like all of team RWBY's field work, as a rule. Particularly Blake kind of works better out on the streets than in a school setting, I feel. In fact, she might even shine there more than in battle. They've really nailed her sense of being slightly different than the others, I think, having a different perspective that they can't have. I like the new outfits, too.<br /> <br /> And the combat. I'll have to watch it again, but shit, so much going down. I utterly love the teamwork they pull off, and to that end, I realised something: Weiss is actually hella good. I hadn't quite seen it before, but Weiss shines in this combat scene. Sure, Ruby is top DPS, and Yang can tank a warmech punch, but Weiss is so much <i>utility</i>. She's support, which is kind of a refreshing place for the &quot;caster&quot; to be. This battle made me see her in a new light combatwise.<br /> <br /> Also, Yang? It's okay. You can say you're actually a Solar. No pressure.<br /> <br /> We got to know that Yang's Semblance is, like, Resistance or something? Some sort of Enrage mechanic? It seems to trigger her SSJ mode, but I'm not sure if it only does that or if it actually reduces incoming damage too. Still, she's by far the tankiest character in the group and so Solar Hero with Resistance it god damn hurts. I might ask what the Christ she was talking about, but that'd be too much of an Exalted forum in-joke.<br /> <br /> So now we know three out of four Semblances, right? Ruby has speed, Weiss has her spell circle platforms, Yang has resistance. I don't think we know what Blake has yet, do we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:17:25-07:00","id":229388,"title":"","content":"OH, and we now know that Sun can make copies of himself. How thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:36:01-07:00","id":229573,"title":"","content":"Blake's is copies too. Hers are solid enough to take hits for her and be used as stepping stones for jumping, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T21:47:18-07:00","id":229949,"title":"","content":"I can't help but notice that in the trailer Sun's team is walking through a urban wasteland, assuming the wasteland isn't just a background and is Haven, it could imply that Haven is a more desolate kingdom. If Cinder's comment that she's from Haven is a truth and not a lie, which we could assume it is or isn't at this point, it could indicate that her plotting involves striking back at the Vale for being the cause of the current state of Haven. This also assumes that she is a form of deposed royalty if Qrows message at the end of last season is interpreted that way and Haven may have been a loser in the great war mentioned in the worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> Or Monty could throw a curveball and it's still too early to guess the master plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3699-zealouscub","name":"zealouscub","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T23:52:27-07:00","id":230048,"title":"","content":"Sooner or later I'll say something on the last episode, I promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:09:54-07:00","id":233050,"title":"","content":"I can't quite make out what Ruby calls the different combat configurations when they fight the Paladin. I had it to something like this:<br /> <br /> Razorburn (12:01) = Weiss + Yang<br /> Checkmate (12:32) = Weiss + Blake<br /> Ladybug (13:05) = Ruby + Blake<br /> Bumblebee (14:00) = Blake + Yang<br /> Ice Flower (14:13) = Weiss + Ruby<br /> <br /> Anyone got anything else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they total Roman's mech which does raise a question that if four Huntresses-in-training are able to take one of those things down, are they really going to stand a chance against full-fledged Hunters and Huntresses?</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of cuts into the question whether team RWBY are representative of the common Huntess student or if they are prodigies of some sort. At least Ruby is implied to be more skilled than the average through her choice of weapon, which Ozpin has pointed out is notoriously difficult to use without slicing yourself to ribbons in the process. While the show does build up towards making Ruby a bit special, the others aren't that far behind, so maybe we can assume that they are better than they really should be.<br /> <br /> Also, the Paladin wasn't in a strong tactical position. Presumably, that big a vehicle is intended to be used with lighter backup units or as part of a bigger force of Paladins for optimal deployment, which Torchwick didn't have in this case. It might therefore have gone down easier than expected.<br /> <br /> All in all, though, it does seem to me that team RWBY's training isn't so much about increasing their power as it is about coordinating it through proper battle tactics. If that is so, then it's believable that a group of students with the right motivation could match a team of &quot;ready&quot; Huntresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:25:58-07:00","id":234720,"title":"","content":"Well it looks like we won't be getting a new episode of RWBY this week. Instead we're getting a <a href=\"http://roosterteeth.com/members/journal/entry.php?id=3244506\" target=\"_blank\">special</a> akin to RvB's PSAs discussing some of the history of Remnant, the world of RWBY.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:34:05-07:00","id":236999,"title":"","content":"According to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v7lsmq4x9fE\" target=\"_blank\">the Q&amp;A livestream</a>, Cinder is 27 years old. So she's pretty much able to pass as a senior student.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T17:41:06-07:00","id":243499,"title":"","content":"Another Thursday, another episode.<br /> <br /> Chapter 5: Extracurricular<br /> <br /> Well things are starting to get <i>interesting</i> at Beacon and I can see more and more of the framework of this season going up.<br /> <br /> We start off with Pyrrha taking on the entirety of Team CRDL which despite Pyrrha clearly being easily one of the top fighters, if not <i>the</i> top fighter, of the class shows that CRDL aren't quite the stereotypical bullies we saw from last season. They are decent fighters at the very least. Of course given what we learn in the following fight and final scene, its clear just how exactly Pyrrha was able to beat them. And all things considering I would like to see how CRDL stacks up against some of the other teams and fighters.<br /> <br /> Then we have the fight that was teased at during the Lazer Team livestream back in June, Pyrrha vs Mercury. Wasn't much of fight as it was pretty clear that Mercury was testing her out for later on when the real combat begins. And like I said, we see Pyrrha using her Semblance and putting together why she is so powerful as a warrior.<br /> <br /> And Blake, Blake, Blake... I've seen this plenty of times before. She's gonna crash and burn at a bad moment in the near future. Anyone else think that she's taking the White Fang's involvement with Torchwick a little too far? I sneaking suspicion that before this season is out we're going to get a flashback or something like that to Blake's younger years when she was in the WF and we'll realize why she's so obsessed with everything right now. My running theories at the moment all revolve around Adam and/or a close family member of Blake in a position of leadership within the new White Fang.<br /> <br /> Beyond that we get another scene of the rest of the team worrying about her and trying to get relax before something inevitably bad happens to her.<br /> <br /> Once again Jaune's back, actually back into the story. His attempt at asking out Weiss was hilariously cringe-worthy. You knew she was going to reject him but it was just so silly you didn't care. And immediately there after we see him training with Pyrrha, showing that yeah he is continuing with what we saw last season and is starting to get decent at it. Like with CRDL I want to see how he stacks up against the others. And it is interesting that they haven't quite figured out Jaune's Semblance. It got me thinking that all we've seen Jaune do with his Aura is that tiny bit of healing and some shielding, the latter of which we know is already a part of what everyone's Aura does but nothing that seems like it could be a Semblance.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately they've continued the annoyingly common trend of Guy is in love with Girl A who doesn't care about him whatsoever, completely oblivious that Girl B actually has feelings for him. God, I've seen that too many times. Really wish I could skip all that to the part where Jaune figures it out and they become a couple.<br /> <br /> Finally we end with Cinder and Co. discussing Pyrrha and her abilities, the last person on a list of people they have some kind of interest in, whether its simply just scouting out the toughest fighters of the competition or something much more nefarious only time will tell. Like I mentioned before they completely revealed Pyrrha's abilities and why she's such a strong fighter. But still nothing on why they're there in the first place. Though I have to say that Cinder's movements seemed... off at times as did some of the lip syncing. I actually had to watch that scene a second time to figure out what she's doing with her hands. She's actually sewing something which probably answers the question about how she manipulates Dust. Though I have to admit the first time I watched it I thought they were going to poison someone or all the people on that list they were compiling. <br /> <br /> All and all another good episode with more of the same, nothing too special but some great teasers of what's to come later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}